      ("Red flags — get medical help",
       "<ul><li>Severe stomach pain that does not go away, with or without vomiting (possible pancreatitis).</li><li>Pain in the upper right abdomen, fever or yellow skin (gallbladder).</li><li>Signs of dehydration or passing much less urine.</li><li>Sudden changes in vision if you have diabetic eye disease.</li></ul>"
       "<p>Before any surgery or procedure with sedation, tell the team you take Ozempic — food can stay in the stomach longer.</p>"),
